<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4898"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->T.FOTH Theory: <BR>Introduction:  Assumptions.  Illusion.  Convolution of evidence over time.  P.T. Barnum.  It’s all here.  Wichita’s BTK has put on quite the show for the past thirty years.  We have all been played - we are indeed, the fiddles of the riddles.  This has all been grand macabre theater, which has sadly now run much longer than “Cats”. <BR> <BR>I cannot say I know who BTK is.  I will not play any potential suspect name games.  That’s all strictly for LE and doesn’t belong here.  I don’t even live in Kansas.   <BR>However, I have reviewed the evidence, read all the postings, and cannot agree with, or produce, an evidentiary-based conclusion that we are looking at a male perp.  In fact, I conclude just the opposite.  The perp is female.  The perp is intelligent, socially accepted, a skilled mental illusionist, and feels intellectually superior to all.  Why?   <BR> <BR>Subject 1:  Semen at the scene:  Basic, simple and fundamental to “the game”.  The Perp’s generation practiced basic birth control &#40;think balloon&#41; and so she most likely had an “unwitting” donor. There was no ejaculation at the scenes, simply the tipping of a jar.  DNA discoveries came much later, so she didn’t realize this was a mistake at the time. It’s a simple ruse for a generally simple audience. &#40;no offense - me included&#41;. <BR>The DNA LE has, or pretends to have, will thus not connect directly to her.  In fact, if married, she can shoot her spouse in the head, call the police, tell them she shot him out of extreme momentary anger because he had admitted to her that he was BTK, show them the “treasure” she has found, the DNA will match, and she would probably walk away with public sympathy, a hero having solved the case. This probably has been her emergency offstage exit plan all along.  Oh Bummer, I guess I just screwed that one up for her.  Anyway, all scripts are written, all acts are rehearsed.  She does have a “special” mind and special talents.  LE is hereby advised. <BR> <BR>Subject 2: The Fox Call: A perp kills 8&#40;?&#41; People and gets away with it over 30 years.  Taunts LE and the public boldly with “cleverness” mixed with some serious BS and self-righteous intellectual superiority.  But, oddly enough, this same perp goes to a very visible public pay phone on a city street and reports the Fox murder.  What’s wrong with this picture?  <BR> <BR>This was neither a mistake by the perp, nor a break in the case.  This was a planned and deliberate illusion, another act in “the play”, only this one “on-stage”, deliberately.  Why?  Audiovisual mind stimulation.  A male voice is heard, and a male suspect is spotted, that was the only purpose.  Therefore, to be contrary to P.T. Barnum’s’ concepts, when the audience’s attention is drawn to something so obvious, look the other direction.  Conclusion: This is a Female perp.  This was a simple “skit”.  Magic 101.   Why this location?  Probably close to work and she was running a little late.  This perp enjoys making things very simple so that her obvious superior intellect provides her self-indulging entertainment.  For those who might be “hung up” on the call itself, had the operator said “did you say 500 main street?” the answer would still have been: “That is correct”.  &#40;Actually would have been beneficial to the perp had the wrong address been confirmed – a entire “hard of hearing” theory would have evolved&#41; <BR> The purpose of the call was not to report a murder, nor a location, both would be discovered anyway.  The purpose of the call was to create an illusion.  The skit was designed to be seen and heard, period.  Note to voice synthesizer experimenters: use “home aside”, play with the punctuation to modify voice inflection, use periods for pauses, “pershing” takes care of itself.  You’ll get it real close with a little tweaking.  Record result into a small recorder – walk to a payphone of your choice, and presto &#40;Females Note: a little dirt on the face for a 5 o’clock shadow, and the right clothes can quickly give you the desired visual affect.&#41;  Amazing.  Damn, It’s magic!   <BR>Note MPD sufferers: you can simply substitute your male voice for the recording above. <BR> <BR>To be continued…as necessary <BR> -T.Foth <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
