<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4926"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 3:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hmmm....interesting theory. <BR> <BR>However, Kevin Bright described a male figure. <BR> <BR>I have a hard time understanding how a female could overpower so many people.  But, then again, I&#39;ve seen some tough-looking ones in the gym. <BR> <BR>What I find a huge stretch is the torture scenario - would a woman torture a child?  I can&#39;t see it.  I know there are likely some gals out there like that - and it would be easy for a woman to enter a home unobserved - but I just can&#39;t pull enough threads out of your theory to wash. <BR> <BR>If you are correct - I will be stunned.  Literally.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
