<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4950"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 7:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Geo: Not sarcastic – appreciate valuable emphasis on “why” the longevity of the production.  <BR> <BR>Pax: Ditto – not spoof – sorry you feel I may be out of bounds or off subject.  Truth is often stranger than fiction.  If I am a waste of your valuable time please ignore me and I apologize.  There is an imaginary little man out there who needs your time. <BR> <BR>Wich: I probably should have left out the MPD option, looks like I’m guilty of some self-entertainment.  I have played with voice synthesizers and I am not on steroids, I don’t even exercise.  Voice programs come on many home PC’s – but may not have during that time.  If you are in Wichita, is there a “telephone co” located in proximity &#40;say 6 blocks max&#41; to the Fox call phone in Wichita? <BR> <BR>Tippy: Thanks for the open mind.  Although if I was putting on a magic show, or was BTK, you’re not one I would necessarily want in the audience.  I don’t believe Bright is BTK related.  By adding this one to the “mix”, evidence becomes convoluted,  For investigative purposes, each crime should be treated as unique and individual anyway, or the same thing can happen.  Vian children I believe too young – Even if they saw what they might have thought was a female, but were ask by LE “Did you see the man?” – the power of suggestion has destroyed any credibility. As far as “overpowering” the victims, I think that is a false assumption.  I don’t believe that was the MO.  I don’t think the victims had any inclination they were “in trouble” until it was too late.  I believe a female would actually be able to pull off this type of “play” much easier than a male.  She would be non-threatening until too late.  “Would a woman torture a child?”  You can’t accept, but you would accept “Why” a man would torture a child?  I see no gender specification with such perversion.  Certainly I understand what the “odds” are, but playing the “odds” just eliminates actual possibilities. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4950-->
<!--Post: 4986--><!--Time: 1106844381-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4986"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 8:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A woman could have strangled the children, but it would have taken a huge amount of upper body strength to kill the adult Oteros. Even a bodybuiler female on lots of steroids would have difficulty strangling Joe and Julie. Just from mindset perspective, one would be more likely to tackle a female with a gun than a male. I am not being chauvinistic since I am female. <BR> <BR>Either way, one would have to be packin&#39; alot of testosterone/aldesterone. She definitely would have a body hair problem. Your topic, though, would being up the issue of adrenal dysfunction, which, for males or females, can mess up the emotions/mind.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
