<!--Post: 5047--><!--Time: 1106856769-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5047"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop: Appreciate the good input. I believe a child could strangle a bound adult to death by twisting a garrote.  It would take less strength than opening a mayonnaise jar.  No big upper body, no body hair problem, no testosterone.  Probably “demure” looking in fact.  Yes, but it would take a lot of strength to bind them?  No, it wouldn’t, not if their hands were already secured behind their back.  But would it not take a lot of strength to get their hands tied behind their back?. My guess is it all actually took no “strength” whatsoever. <BR> <BR>Nancydrew:   Thanks much, although to stay with my theme of “very simple”, I think PJ’s just means pajamas - lace, frilly treasures.  Nothing more, nothing less. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
