<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5120"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 6:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->---&#34;However, I have reviewed the evidence, read all the postings, and cannot agree with, or produce, an evidentiary-based conclusion that we are looking at a male perp.&#34;  <BR>--Just curious, Tfoth, how can you say this? The <BR>Vian children, the eldest of which was 8 years of age- described the perp as a dark complected <BR>male with a moustache.  Approximately 30 years of age with a paunchy belly. The police sketch shown on Crime Library is based on the Vian&#39;s witness.  Even BTK says that the only witnesses he left were the Vian children.  Bear in mind, he started to tie-up the eldest boy, and then proceeded to herd all 3 children in to the bathroom.  Based on this evidence alone, how can you NOT reach an &#34;evidentiary-based conclusion&#34; that we ARE looking at a male perp?  Are you sure <BR>you have read all the early articles?  I am not <BR>trying to be unkind, but this is absolutely the <BR>most preposterous theory I have ever heard.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
