<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5159"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 8:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My apologies to all for this thread.  I come from a world where colleagues and peers have names, facial expressions, and voices.  So as you might imagine, I find myself very uncomfortable in this realm, which I so innocently entered.  For this final post, I will try to be concise and clinical, knowing I risk cryptic diagnosis regardless.  I shall then politely excuse myself from further participation.   <BR> <BR>I believe this is all going to end very soon anyway, thankfully, due to the SK’S recent crescendo of activities, I believe designed to gather the audience for the final curtain call.  And yes George, those are theater references, because THAT’S EXACTLY WHAT THIS HAS BEEN! <BR> <BR>I posted a legitimate theory on an internet message board, and used a little creative writing to get things started, looking for legitimate discussion, and knowing LE most likely monitors these things, to put the possibility before them.  That George, contrary to believing I might be intelligent, actually proves I am an idiot.  Ref: Results of this thread. <BR> <BR>My interest in this SK stems from the unique complexity of the disorders.  The most intriguing, and I think “telling” being the off the charts and never before seen magnitude of the Histrionic Personality Disorder.  I believe the SK to be a volatile and possibly never before seen formula of disorders that will be in textbooks for centuries.   <BR>1. MPD with 1 if not more “male” personalities, one being your BTK.   <BR>2. Necromancy – the intimacy of the death experience  <BR>3. Add to the above the overriding Histrionic Personality Disorder. <BR>Verm: Your “odds” input was good.  However, should the MPD above be correct, we would be applying them to the male personality so they would be positive.  In addition, if we want to play odds, if we consider the formula above, WHO is most often affected, and WHEN such disorders most typically manifest themselves in life, coupled with the BTK timeline, then the odds-on favorite becomes: Your BTK is now going to turn out to be a 70-80 yr old woman. <BR> <BR>Curious2:  I backed off the theory and “stood corrected” with your factual evidence of the Vian children describing a man.  Hoping to just disappear.  I was actually aware of this evidence and obviously I could have used the same information to reinforce my theory by simply replying “Ah, and that would explain why the SK let them live…..”, because they had seen “the man” that would be a “good thing” for the SK. <BR> <BR>Because the Histrionic Personality Disorder seems to have total control and overrides the thought processes of the host, I believe the victims were chosen because the SK somehow witnessed them getting attention.  That, in the SK’s mind, would be a capital offense. <BR> <BR>Wich: in reply to your reply, I was just trying to be conversational. <BR>Geo: Considering the enormous amount of time and effort you have spent analyzing “the most asinine thing you have ever read” I can’t imagine how focused you might become when you are soon freed of these activities and allowed the time to just read a good book. <BR> <BR>Ok, I’m done.  I hope this all ends soon and many herein are set free.  <BR>It has been….a truly unique and memorable experience. <BR>I must now return to real life. <BR>-T.Foth <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5159-->
<!--Post: 5173--><!--Time: 1106935255-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5173"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nancydrew<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nancydrew<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 10:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tfoth:  I thought you made sense....I think it&#39;s far fetched, and the odds are really slim that BTK will end up being a woman, but it&#39;s a topic worth review.  Sorry to see you go. <BR> <BR>George:  If you don&#39;t like it, skip the thread.  You&#39;re acting like the message board monitor / tattler.  Take a deep breath, step away from the keyboard, and lighten up.  We don&#39;t have to have your opinion on every single statement made on these boards.  Now go tell Tom that Nancydrew is talkin&#39; crazy!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
