<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5178"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 10:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TFOTH, <BR> <BR>There is nothing wrong with thinking “outside the box.”  There is also there is nothing wrong with challenging someone’s ideas.  This is precisely how research moves along and why this forum exists. <BR> <BR>There could be a possibility of BTK dressing like a woman &#40;just in the instances of when he is in public, gaining entrance into a home, or staging his getaway&#41;.  <BR> <BR>I think somebody on this forum said he carried of bag of stuff with him -- his disguise? <BR> <BR>NancyDrew: <BR>Thank you for your observation about PJ.  I thought EXACTLY the same thing, however I simply didn’t know how to word it.  You did that beautifully.   <BR> <BR>I don’t know why this bothers ME &#40;ONLY&#41;, but the children described him/her as having a pot belly?  I find that a really weird observation.  Of course, the children were probably eye-level to his/her belly – so I guess that is why/how they noted it. <BR> <BR>A pot belly on someone who is in shape enough to overpower the Oteros?  &#40;Okay, you argue that even an 80-year-old grandmother could overpower someone as long as she brandishes a gun.&#41;  Point well taken. <BR> <BR>How often do you see pot bellies on young adults supposedly at BTK’s age at the time?  Pot bellies seem to develop at later ages in life.  &#40;I put on another thread that perhaps the bot belly was indeed his “aroused appendage” and perhaps the children noted the “bulge.” <BR> <BR>BUT -- go easy on me on this one -- but did anybody ever think “SHE” could be pregnant, or feigning a woman that is pregnant?   <BR> <BR>Not a bad ruse indeed – who would ever think they were going to get clocked by a pregnant female &#40;or someone dressed like one&#41;?   <BR> <BR>Count me in on thinking a pregnant female is generally pretty harmless.   <BR> <BR>And don’t ask me why the “pot belly” detail bugs me – it just does!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
