<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tfoth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tfoth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->T.FOTH THEORY VERSION G: <BR>For this gender-neutral version of the theory we will disregard that female MPD sufferers outnumber men by a ratio of nine to one &#40;Hales, 1993&#41;.  This should get us past the obvious aversion to a female perp. <BR> <BR>With the original theory the psychological profile presented was: <BR>Female Host &#43; MPD &#43; Necromancy &#43; HPD = BTK <BR>Remove the Female host from the equation  <BR>MPD &#43; Necromancy &#43; HPD = BTK <BR>Now let’s refine it further to: <BR> <BR>MPD&#40;3&#41; &#43; Necromancy&#40;3&#41; &#43; HPD = BTK <BR> <BR>The reason for the qualification is that only 1 of the 3 personas is BTK, we’ll call it “3” just for illustration, and “3” is also the only one that has a fetish with the intimacy of the death experience.  To keep it simple with just 3 personas, “1” will be the outward, recorded, known person, “2” will be just another persona for kicks, and “3” is the one known as BTK.  Let’s assume that the MPD stems from a traumatic childhood incident that manifested itself inside the host, oh let’s say about 1949.  At the same time, an associated disorder was induced which resulted in an intense need for attention &#40;Histrionic Personality Disorder&#41;, this most likely resulting from careless and flawed care in the aftermath of the child’s trauma.  The HPD is omnipresent, crossing over all personas and thus the underlying and overriding control mechanism of the individual. <BR> <BR>Submitted for your consideration: <BR>BTK is an enigma.  It is possible that BTK is nothing but an imaginary man that does not, and never has, actually existed as a “recorded person”.  It is possible that BTK is not a being at all, but instead BTK is actually an “EVENT”.   <BR>In other words, BTK is not a person, “BTK Happens”. <BR>Now, could this “BTK” have a birth certificate?  A social security number?   A job history?   Could this BTK have served in the Military?  Is it possible that the only people who have ever actually witnessed “BTK” face to face have been murdered?   <BR>And if that is possible, what do “profiles” of BTK provide?  Possibly nothing at all.   <BR>It is possible that the actual profile of BTK might turn out to be:  <BR>A professional, socially active civic minded individual that has given much to charity and is active in many church organizations as well as volunteering much time to the needy.  Has been married for….. years and  has…. kids…. Often works behind the scenes at Thanksgiving dinners for the homeless.  Became an ordained Minister in…..  Was Scoutmaster for….  Has funded numerous…. Works tirelessly for orphans…. Heads the annual Christmas……  does volunteer work for…. and…. and…. and… <BR> <BR>There now, oh my, that should light a few fuses.    <BR>Lock and Load!   Incoming!!!! <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
