<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6298"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TFoth:  I&#39;m not going to knock the theory you&#39;ve presented.  Your argument is logically sound.  I guess we won&#39;t know her/his gender for sure unless &#34;BTK&#34; is found. I&#39;m also fascinated by the MPD aspect of your theory.  &#34;BTK is not a person, BTK happens.&#34;  BTK stated in his original letter to WPD that a &#34;monster&#34; was actually running the game.   <BR> <BR>I&#39;m aware that MPD has been presented as an explanation in criminal cases before.  I don&#39;t know if any researchers have ever confirmed that a person with MPD could have a homicidal alter &#34;personality state&#34; &#40;for lack of a better phrase&#41;.  However, in my opinion, no one has ever demonstrated why it couldn&#39;t be possible.   <BR> <BR>Why would LE and the psychiatric establishment be reluctant to accept a connection between MPD and homicidal behaviour?  &#40;Aside from the issue of malingerers claiming to have MPD.&#41;  It may, in fact, be another factor to consider in developing a profile.  I wonder what the latest research on this is...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
